cache/*
!cache/.gitkeep
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pkl
build.log

# session-start hook artefacts
.claude/hooks/*.log

# Binder and invoice attachments. A PDF attachment is evidence that is sighted and screened, not
# a repository artefact: the corpus retains page_text, the M1 verdict is retained in each batch's
# mask_screen_<batch>.json, and the binder md5 is recorded in both. Re-parsing a batch needs the
# binder re-supplied, which is the accepted trade.
*.pdf

# Not attachments: the two standing Council reference documents the JSON captures in
# data/reference/ were made from, and the authority those captures are verified against.
!data/reference/*.pdf

# Build OUTPUTS. The test is reproducibility, not size: a file a script here rebuilds is an output and does
# not belong in history, because an xlsx is a zip git cannot delta-compress and a version committed once costs
# its full size in every clone forever. 23 registers in one week came to 288 MB, cleared only by rewriting
# history. Everything needed to rebuild these IS tracked: the TechOne inputs, the corpora, the briefs and
# match tables, and the one register no script here can produce.
registers/*.xlsx
!registers/PS_WP_Transaction_Register_3FY_v127_CANDIDATE.xlsx
reports/*.xlsx
